@startuml
' Domain detail; ModelClassDiagram shows the API and record containers.
!define MODEL_COLOR #9D0012
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam arrowThickness 1.1
skinparam arrowColor MODEL_COLOR
skinparam classBackgroundColor MODEL_COLOR
skinparam class {
    FontColor #FFFFFF
    FontSize 16
    BorderThickness 1
    BorderColor #FFFFFF
    StereotypeFontColor #FFFFFF
    FontName Arial
    AttributeFontColor #FFFFFF
    AttributeFontSize 15
    AttributeFontName Arial
}
skinparam noteFontSize 14
skinparam DefaultTextAlignment center
skinparam Shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 80
skinparam ranksep 65
hide circle
hide empty members
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
left to right direction

title Model records: fields, ownership, and appointment snapshots

class Client {
    - name: ClientName
    - phone: Phone
    - email: Email
    - address: Address
    - tags: Tag [0..*]
}

class Pet {
    - name: PetName
    - species: Species
    - breed: Breed [0..1]
    - requirement: Requirement
}

class Appointment {
    - date: AppointmentDate
    - startTime: StartTime
    - endTime: EndTime
    - service: Service
}

' Participant references are shown only as associations, not duplicated as attributes.
Appointment "0..*" -right-> "1\npet" Pet
Pet "0..*" -right-> "1\nowner" Client
Appointment "0..*" --> "1\nowner" Client

note bottom of Client
  Client, Pet, and Appointment are immutable.
  Edits replace complete record objects.
  Clients are unique by phone OR email.
end note

note bottom of Pet
  Pet identity: owner phone + normalized name.
  Names ignore case and surrounding/repeated spaces.
  Each registered pet references its saved client.
  Species and Service are enumeration types.
end note

note top of Appointment
  The owner must match the pet's owner.
  Duration is at least 30 minutes.
  Participants are immutable snapshots and may share
  objects with the registered client and pet lists.
end note

@enduml
